<!-- 
1. type="submit"
<button type="submit">Submit</button>

Purpose: Submit the form.

When clicked:

click button
   ↓
form submit event
   ↓
form data is sent

In your code:

form.addEventListener("submit", ...)

will run.

2. type="button"
<button type="button">Reset Password</button>

Purpose: Just a normal button.

It does not submit the form.

You can attach your own JavaScript:

button.addEventListener("click", () => {
    window.location.href = "/form/reset";
});

So this is what you want for your Reset Password button.

3. type="reset"
<button type="reset">Reset</button>

Purpose: Reset the form's inputs to their original values.

For example:

<form>
    <input value="hello">
    <input value="12345">

    <button type="reset">Reset</button>
</form> -->